			<div class="c-things-to-do-post-contents js-things-to-do-post-contents">
				<div id="description" class="c-things-to-do-post-thumb-area js-target-contents">
				<div class="c-things-to-do-post-thumb is-fade js-fade-anime">
						<div class="swiper slider js-slider-things-to-do-post-thumb">
		<div class="swiper-wrapper c-things-to-do-post-thumb__slide-wrapper">
		<div class="swiper-slide c-things-to-do-post-thumb__slide"><img class="c-things-to-do-post-thumb__img lazyload" src="data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAyAAAAJYAQMAAACguBAzAAAAA1BMVEUAAACnej3aAAAAAXRSTlMAQObYZgAAAFBJREFUGBntwQEBAAAAgqD+r3ZIwAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAADgQOy4AAFERiVmAAAAAElFTkSuQmCC" alt="" data-src="https://d1ixxqrn2t5gu0.cloudfront.net/wp/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/報国寺.jpg" decoding="async" data-eio-rwidth="800" data-eio-rheight="600"><noscript><img class="c-things-to-do-post-thumb__img" src="https://d1ixxqrn2t5gu0.cloudfront.net/wp/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/報国寺.jpg" alt="" data-eio="l"></noscript></div>		</div>
				</div>


		<div class="swiper slider-thumbnail js-slider-things-to-do-post-thumbnail">
			<div class="swiper-wrapper c-things-to-do-post-thumb__lists">
			<div class="swiper-slide"><img class="c-things-to-do-post-thumb__img lazyload" src="data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAKUAAABuAQMAAAB8ykHuAAAAA1BMVEUAAACnej3aAAAAAXRSTlMAQObYZgAAABlJREFUGBljGAWjYBSMglEwCkbBKBgFNAcACXQAAYFzY1cAAAAASUVORK5CYII=" alt="" data-src="https://d1ixxqrn2t5gu0.cloudfront.net/wp/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/報国寺-165x110.jpg" decoding="async" data-eio-rwidth="165" data-eio-rheight="110"><noscript><img class="c-things-to-do-post-thumb__img" src="https://d1ixxqrn2t5gu0.cloudfront.net/wp/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/報国寺-165x110.jpg" alt="" data-eio="l"></noscript></div>			</div>
		</div>
						<div class="c-things-to-do-post-thumb__desc"><p>The temple has always been known for the Moso bamboo forest in its precinct, which is why Hokokuji is also called the Bamboo Temple. The principal image is a statue of a seated Shakanyorai. The founder, Tengan Eko, studied in China during the Yuan Dynasty (1271-1368). Tokishu, the autograph collection of his poems, is an important national cultural asset.</p>
</div>				</div>
									<div id="basic-info" class="c-things-to-do-post-basic js-target-contents">
						<h2 class="c-things-to-do-post-basic__ttl is-fade js-fade-anime">Basic Information</h2>
						<table class="c-things-to-do-post-basic__table is-fade js-fade-anime">
															<tr class="c-things-to-do-post-basic__tr">
									<th class="c-things-to-do-post-basic__th">
										Address									</th>
									<td class="c-things-to-do-post-basic__td">
																					<p>2-7-4 Jomyoji, Kamakura city</p>
																			</td>
								</tr>
															<tr class="c-things-to-do-post-basic__tr">
									<th class="c-things-to-do-post-basic__th">
										Access									</th>
									<td class="c-things-to-do-post-basic__td">
																					<p>From the JR Kamakura Station East Exit bus stop, take the bus bound for Jomyoji and get off at Jomyoji. 3 minutes walk</p>
<p>Or, 35 minutes walk from JR Kamakura Station</p>
																			</td>
								</tr>
															<tr class="c-things-to-do-post-basic__tr">
									<th class="c-things-to-do-post-basic__th">
										Phone									</th>
									<td class="c-things-to-do-post-basic__td">
																					<p>0467-22-0762</p>
																			</td>
								</tr>
															<tr class="c-things-to-do-post-basic__tr">
									<th class="c-things-to-do-post-basic__th">
										Fees									</th>
									<td class="c-things-to-do-post-basic__td">
																					<p>【Admission fee】<br />
High school students and above: 400 yen<br />
Elementary and junior high school students: 200 yen<br />
*Matcha tea voucher (includes dried sweets): 600 yen<br />
Disabled: Free (disability certificate required)<br />
Seniors living in the city: Free (Fukuju certificate required)</p>
																			</td>
								</tr>
															<tr class="c-things-to-do-post-basic__tr">
									<th class="c-things-to-do-post-basic__th">
										Business Hours									</th>
									<td class="c-things-to-do-post-basic__td">
																					<p>9:00am-4:00pm<br />
*Matcha tea reception closes at 3:30pm<br />
*Closed from December 29th to January 3rd</p>
																			</td>
								</tr>
															<tr class="c-things-to-do-post-basic__tr">
									<th class="c-things-to-do-post-basic__th">
										Note									</th>
									<td class="c-things-to-do-post-basic__td">
																					<p>◆ Experience<br />
【Tea】<br />
Drink matcha tea on a chair in the bamboo garden<br />
Dates: Every day (closed over the New Year holidays)<br />
Time: 9:00am-4:00pm (reception until 3:30pm)<br />
Price: 600 yen for matcha tea with dried sweets (bamboo garden admission fee required)<br />
*No reservation required<br />
*Matcha reception may be temporarily suspended during peak hours</p>
<p>【Sunday Zazen Session】<br />
This is a strict Zazen session, so please come prepared.<br />
Date: Every Sunday (open all year round)<br />
Time: 7:30am-9:15am<br />
Registration: 7:00am-7:30am (strict timekeeping)<br />
*In principle, leaving midway is not permitted<br />
*Please wear loose clothing that is easy to move in. In summer, you may sweat, so we recommend bringing a towel and a change of clothes.<br />
*As a rule, this Zazen session will be conducted in Japanese. Interpretation will not be provided during the session.<br />
*The session may be canceled due to weather, etc. (If there are any changes to the session, we will announce them on the official website)</p>
<p>◆Other<br />
・Tripods, monopods, selfie sticks, etc. are prohibited.<br />
・Public toilets available.</p>
																			</td>
								</tr>
													</table>
					</div>
				
